    <div class="tldr"><p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> card counting means keeping a running tally of the cards dealt so you know when the remaining deck is rich in high cards, which favour the player. In Hi-Lo, 2–6 count +1 and tens and aces count −1. It’s legal, but the edge is small, it demands real discipline, and it doesn’t work online.</p></div>
